    <h2>What Is the Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard delivers a three-layered flavor experience: crunchy roasted pecans, sweet caramel, and warm hot fudge — all distributed throughout DQ's smooth vanilla soft serve. It is one of the slightly pricier standard Blizzards at $3.99 Mini (vs. $3.49 for Oreo or Butterfinger), reflecting the higher ingredient cost of whole pecans.</p>
  <p>Find this and all other DQ items on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a> or browse the complete <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats</a> list.</p>

    <h2>Why the Turtle Blizzard Is for Nut Lovers</h2>
  <p>Most Blizzards use candy bars or cookie pieces as mix-ins. The Turtle Pecan Cluster stands apart because it uses whole pecans — actual roasted nuts, not nut-flavored pieces. Combined with caramel and hot fudge, this creates a texture and flavor profile closer to a premium sundae than a candy-bar Blizzard.</p>
  <p>If you enjoy the <a href="/items/peanut-buster-parfait">Peanut Buster Parfait</a> (which also features nuts + fudge), the Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard is the closest Blizzard equivalent — just with caramel added and pecans instead of peanuts.</p>
  <h2>Allergen Note</h2>
  <p>The Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard contains <strong>tree nuts (pecans)</strong> in addition to the standard milk and soy allergens. If you or someone in your group has a tree nut allergy, choose a nut-free Blizzard such as the <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo</a> or <a href="/items/smores-blizzard">S'mores Blizzard</a>.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Turtle Pecan Cluster</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>570</td><td>Nuts + caramel + fudge, complex</td></tr><tr><td>Brownie Batter Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>530</td><td>Rich chocolate, no nuts</td></tr><tr><td>Peanut Buster Parfait</td><td class="price-cell">$4.99 (parfait)</td><td>710</td><td>Peanuts + fudge in a cup</td></tr><tr><td>Choco Brownie Extreme</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>510</td><td>Brownie + fudge</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (3.99) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (4.79) at 570 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

